✔ Auto-fetch from GitHub
    It checks for updates automatically every few minutes.
        To enable:
            Open VS Code
            Press Ctrl + ,
            Search: git autofetch
            Turn it ON
            (Optional) Run: git pull

✔ How collaborators push to the repository
    After cloning:
        git clone <repo-url>
        cd <repo-folder>

    Ensure they are on main:
        git checkout main

    If main does not exist locally:
        git checkout -b main origin/main

    Set upstream (only needed once per machine):
        git push --set-upstream origin main

    After this, pushing changes is simply:
        git add .
        git commit -m "{CHANGE DETAILS - INITIALS}"
        git push

FOR UPLOADING GIT CHANGES:
    How to manage your .gitignore going forward:
        git add .gitignore
        git commit -m "Update .gitignore"
        git push

    How to manage ALL git changes:
        git add .
        git commit -m "{ADD CHANGE DETAILS - INITIALS}"
        git push
